  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two salts <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>MX</mi></math> have the same value of solubility product of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The ratio of their molar solubilizes i.e. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>MX</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;________.</p><p>(Round off to the Nearest Integer).</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "50",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8594;</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>+</mo></mtd><mtd><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd/><mtd/><mtd><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd/><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi>sp</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msubsup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>MX</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>MX</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8594;</mo></mtd><mtd><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>+</mo></mtd><mtd><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd/><mtd/><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd/><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi>sp</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>So <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi>MX</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></math></p>",
